.TH XZTOP 1 "1 November 2026" "amix-z3660rtg" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xztop \- the Z3660's temperatures and voltages in an X window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xztop
[
.B \-update
.I seconds
] [
.B \-device
.I file
] [
.I toolkit options
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xztop
shows the measurements the Z3660 accelerator's firmware makes, the ones
.BR ztop (1)
prints, as small strip charts in the manner of
.BR xload (1):
the 68060, FPGA and board temperatures and the 5 V, 3.3 V and FPGA core
voltages, each under a line with its latest value, and the CPU clock the
preset sets at the top.
A temperature chart draws a scale line every 10 degrees Celsius, a voltage
chart one every volt.
A measurement the firmware does not offer gets no chart.
.PP
The charts move every two seconds.
Each reads the RTG driver's information node
.IR /dev/zz9000i ,
which any user may open (falling back to
.IR /dev/zz9000 ),
and the board is read at most once a second however many charts there are.
.B xztop
writes nothing to the board.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-update " seconds"
Move the charts every
.I seconds
(1 to 60; the default is 2).
.TP
.BI \-device " file"
Read this device instead.
.PP
The X Toolkit options
.RB ( \-display ,
.BR \-geometry ,
.BR \-fg ,
.BR \-bg ,
.B \-xrm
and the rest) apply.
.SH RESOURCES
The class is
.BR XZtop .
.TP
.B update
as
.BR \-update .
.TP
.B device
as
.BR \-device .
.PP
The labels are named
.BR clock ,
.BR cpu ,
.BR fpga ,
.BR board ,
.BR v5 ,
.B v3v3
and
.BR vcore ;
each chart has its label's name.
The StripChart resources
.RB ( foreground ,
.BR highlight ,
.BR width ,
.BR height )
set the charts' look, for example
.RS
.nf
XZtop*StripChart.height: 48
XZtop*cpu.foreground: red
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
1 when the device cannot be opened, 2 for a usage error, 3 when the board
offers no sensors (a ZZ9000, or Z3660 firmware without them).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /dev/zz9000i
the RTG driver's information node (character 49, minor 128, mode 0444)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ztop (1),
.BR xload (1)
